feat(auth): custom OTP email verification + homepage CTAs

Replaces Supabase Auth's magic-link verification with our own 6-digit
code flow so users finish signup inside our UI instead of clicking an
external email link.

- Migration 008_pending_signups.sql: short-lived staging table holding
  encrypted password + bcrypt OTP hash + attempts + expiry (15 min).
- lib/auth/crypt.ts: AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt keyed off JWT_SECRET,
  plus a uniform-random 6-digit OTP generator.
- /api/auth/signup: generates an OTP, encrypts password, upserts the
  pending row, emails the code (via Gmail/Nodemailer). Cooldown 30s,
  refuses if a verified profile already exists.
- /api/auth/verify-email: validates OTP (5 attempts max), creates the
  Supabase auth user via admin.createUser({ email_confirm: true }),
  back-fills profiles, then signInWithPassword on the cookie-bound
  server client to set the session and land them on /dashboard.
- /api/auth/resend-verification: regenerates + re-emails the OTP with
  the same cooldown, returns a generic message to avoid email
  enumeration.
- /auth/signup page: redirects to /auth/verify-email?email=... after
  the signup POST succeeds.
- /auth/verify-email page: 6-input OTP field with paste / arrow-key /
  backspace handling, resend button with live countdown, auto-redirect
  to /dashboard once verified + signed-in.
- Site header (public marketing site): adds "Sign in" + "Dashboard"
  links in the desktop nav and mobile drawer so visitors can find the
  SaaS without guessing the routes.

Run lib/db/migrations/008_pending_signups.sql in Supabase SQL editor
before deploying.
